	spec: 'Invariant: accepting a path does not enroll it in file-change tracking. File tools and Bash modifies accept valid absolute and relative paths in every directory, including parent-relative paths. Track declared project files beneath cwd and files beneath /tmp only; exclude .git metadata and other outside-cwd files, including symlink aliases whose canonical target is excluded. Excluded Bash declarations produce no copies, changed-file entries, declaration locks or neighbor notices and never prevent the command from running. Broad globs filter excluded matches. WRITE and EDIT still take canonical file locks everywhere for atomic lease-safe operations, while their change tracking follows the same scope. Sensitive eligible files retain metadata only. Preserve independent commit notices. Tool help distinguishes accepted inputs from tracked files. Tests cover accepted untracked writes, .git and symlink exclusions, eligible project and /tmp files, globs and lock behavior. User clarification on 9 Oct 2026 corrects den: all directories are accessible, not all directories are tracked.',
